    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d761">

                <pb facs="0870" n="750" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg750"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                        Meyer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-06-27"><hi rendition="#italic">June 27,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 43.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copy of a letter from the
                    Standard Oil Company of New York,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d761-f1"/> presenting’ a
                    claim for the seizure and destruction by the Russian naval authorities of a
                    cargo of petroleum shipped by the company from New York to Yokohama on board the
                    English steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Oldhamia.</hi></p>
                <p>Upon the facts stated it appears to the Department that the Russian Government is
                    clearly liable to make compensation to the claimant for the value of the cargo,
                    which is accordingly requested.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert H. D.
                    Peirce.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
